<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reinhard von Dalwigk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1802">1802</a>–<a href="/years/1880">1880</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reinhard von Dalwigk was chief minister of the Grand Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> from 1850 to 1871. After the revolution of 1848 he restored conservative government and pursued an anti-Prussian policy, siding with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in the war of 1866 and hoping for French support. Hesse nevertheless fought on the German side in 1870 and joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>, and he left office in 1871.</p></div>
